                <pb facs="0519" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5805: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-12-02T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                                1924—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 2—3:33
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>466. My number 465, December 1, 4 p.m. Chang Tso-lin without warning left Peking
                    December 2, 4 a.m., I am informed, for Tientsin taking headquarters staff and
                    bodyguard. Sun Fo and other Kuomintang leaders in Peking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
